      "side": 1,
      "message": "No everything is spawning a go routine within \"parseHeader\", eg: OFPTFlowMod is a blocking operation.\n\nMy assumption was that the operations that are treated asynchronously in \"parseHeader\" were operations that can be the run in the background. From what I can see the only requests that spawn a new thread are not really operation on traffic but really control messages like Get/SetConfigRequest, PacketIn/Out and Role changes.\n\nThe point of this patch is to guarantee that a batch of instructions are processed (namely sent to the core) before we start processing a new batch (basically honoring the BarrierRequest).",
